      "content": "TL 01 SE                    REDBOURN             HEMEL HEMPSTEAD ROAD                                                  (south east side)                                                  REDBOURN 4/170                                            Flowers Farmhouse II Farmhouse.   C17 timber frame,  recased   in red brick c.1830. Plain tile roof.   Dentilled brick eaves.   2 storeys.   3 windows, those of upper floor long Yorkshire casements with small glazing bar panes.  Ground floor has 3 broad openings with good gauged brick lintels, the door on right.   Early stack behind this door. Rear elevation with 3 similar casements in flush moulded frames. Half-bay late C19 extension on NW end. Listing NGR: TL0997111041"
    }
